@namespace Blaizio.Ui
@using System.Globalization
@*
    Styled color input group - one bordered container holding an optional swatch dot and either a
    single free-text field (hex, or Channels off) or per-channel fields (every other format:
    329° | 86% | 70%, hairline-divided). The text field accepts ANY parseable color on change
    (blur / Enter) - every supported format, hex without the #, a bare "r g b" list - auto-detected
    and converted. Channel edits rebuild the color keeping the other channels at full precision.
    Invalid entries are dropped.
*@

<div data-slot="color-input-group"
     class="@Tw.Merge(GroupClasses, Class)"
     @attributes="Attributes">
    @if (ShowSwatch)
    {
        <span class="flex items-center ps-2" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="size-4 shrink-0 rounded-full border border-black/10" style="@DotStyle"></span>
        </span>
    }
    @if (UseChannels)
    {
        var raw = RawComponents();
        var labels = ChannelLabels();
        <div class="divide-input flex min-w-0 grow items-stretch divide-x">
            @for (var i = 0; i < raw.Length; i++)
            {
                var index = i;
                var spec = Spec(index);
                <BzInputNumber TValue="double"
                               Value="@Parse(raw[index])"
                               ValueChanged="value => OnChannelValue(index, value)"
                               Min="@spec.Min"
                               Max="@spec.Max"
                               Step="@spec.Step"
                               LargeStep="@(spec.Step * 10)"
                               Format="@spec.Format"
                               Culture="System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture"
                               Buttons="false"
                               Disabled="@Context!.Disabled"
                               Label="@labels[index]"
                               Class="h-full min-w-0 flex-1 rounded-none border-0 bg-transparent shadow-none focus-within:ring-0"
                               FieldClass="px-1 text-center font-mono"
                               Attributes="_channelAttributes" />
            }
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <input value="@Display"
               @onchange="OnChange"
               type="text"
               spellcheck="false"
               autocomplete="off"
               autocorrect="off"
               autocapitalize="off"
               disabled="@Context!.Disabled"
               aria-label="@AriaLabel"
               data-slot="color-input"
               class="@TextClasses" />
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Show the value in this format instead of the picker's. Defaults to the picker's format.</summary>
    [Parameter] public ColorFormat? Format { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Show the current-color dot at the start of the group. Defaults to <c>false</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool ShowSwatch { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Per-channel fields for non-hex formats (hex always keeps the free-text field). Defaults to <c>true</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Channels { get; set; } = true;

    /// <summary>Accessible name for the free-text field. Defaults to <c>"Color value"</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string AriaLabel { get; set; } = "Color value";

    /// <summary>Extra classes, merged over the group's defaults.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Any other attributes, forwarded to the group element.</summary>
    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)] public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? Attributes { get; set; }

    [CascadingParameter] private ColorPickerContext? Context { get; set; }

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (Context is null)
            throw new InvalidOperationException($"{nameof(BzColorInput)} must be placed inside a {nameof(BzColorPicker)}.");
    }

    private ColorFormat EffectiveFormat => Format ?? Context!.Format;

    private bool UseChannels => Channels && EffectiveFormat != ColorFormat.Hex;

    private string Display =>
        ColorMath.Format(Context!.H, Context.S, Context.V, Context.EffectiveA, EffectiveFormat);

    private string DotStyle =>
        $"background-image:linear-gradient({Context!.Css}, {Context.Css}), {BzColorAlphaSlider.Checkerboard};" +
        "background-size:auto, 6px 6px;background-color:#fff";

    // ---- channel plumbing -----------------------------------------------------------------------

    // The color's own serialization (alpha stripped - opacity lives with the alpha slider) is the
    // source of the channel values, so display and rebuild can never drift from ColorMath.
    private string[] RawComponents()
    {
        var text = ColorMath.Format(Context!.H, Context.S, Context.V, 1, EffectiveFormat);
        var body = text[(text.IndexOf('(') + 1)..^1];
        var parts = body.Split([',', ' '], StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries | StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);
        // rgba()/hsla() always serialize four components - the fourth is the alpha we stripped to 1.
        var count = EffectiveFormat == ColorFormat.Cmyk ? 4 : 3;
        return parts[..Math.Min(count, parts.Length)];
    }

    private string[] ChannelLabels() => EffectiveFormat switch
    {
        ColorFormat.Rgb or ColorFormat.Rgba => ["Red", "Green", "Blue"],
        ColorFormat.Hsl or ColorFormat.Hsla => ["Hue", "Saturation", "Lightness"],
        ColorFormat.Hsb => ["Hue", "Saturation", "Brightness"],
        ColorFormat.Hwb => ["Hue", "Whiteness", "Blackness"],
        ColorFormat.Cmyk => ["Cyan", "Magenta", "Yellow", "Black"],
        ColorFormat.Oklch => ["Lightness", "Chroma", "Hue"],
        _ => ["Lightness", "A axis", "B axis"],
    };

    private static readonly IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object> _channelAttributes =
        new PropBuilder().Data("slot", "color-channel").Merge(null);

    private readonly record struct ChannelSpec(double Min, double Max, double Step, string Format);

    // Domain + display per channel: degrees and percents step by 1 and read as integers with their
    // suffix (a quoted literal in the .NET format, so '%' doesn't trigger the multiply-by-100
    // semantic); the perceptual oklch/oklab magnitudes step finely and keep decimals.
    private ChannelSpec Spec(int index) => EffectiveFormat switch
    {
        ColorFormat.Rgb or ColorFormat.Rgba => new(0, 255, 1, "0"),
        ColorFormat.Hsl or ColorFormat.Hsla or ColorFormat.Hsb or ColorFormat.Hwb =>
            index == 0 ? new(0, 360, 1, "0'°'") : new(0, 100, 1, "0'%'"),
        ColorFormat.Cmyk => new(0, 100, 1, "0'%'"),
        ColorFormat.Oklch => index switch
        {
            0 => new(0, 1, 0.01, "0.###"),
            1 => new(0, 0.4, 0.01, "0.###"),
            _ => new(0, 360, 1, "0'°'"),
        },
        _ => index == 0 ? new(0, 1, 0.01, "0.###") : new(-0.4, 0.4, 0.01, "0.###"),
    };

    private async Task OnChannelValue(int index, double? value)
    {
        if (value is not double next) return;

        // Replace only the edited component; the others keep their full-precision serialized form.
        var raw = RawComponents();
        raw[index] = raw[index].EndsWith('%')
            ? next.ToString("0.##", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + "%"
            : next.ToString("0.###", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);

        var rebuilt = $"{FunctionName()}({string.Join(' ', raw)})";
        if (!ColorMath.TryParse(rebuilt, out var h, out var s, out var v, out _))
            return;
        await Context!.Root.SetAsync(h, s, v, Context.A);
        await Context.Root.CommitAsync();
    }

    private string FunctionName() => EffectiveFormat switch
    {
        ColorFormat.Rgb or ColorFormat.Rgba => "rgb",
        ColorFormat.Hsl or ColorFormat.Hsla => "hsl",
        ColorFormat.Hsb => "hsb",
        ColorFormat.Hwb => "hwb",
        ColorFormat.Cmyk => "device-cmyk",
        ColorFormat.Oklch => "oklch",
        _ => "oklab",
    };

    private static double Parse(string component) =>
        double.TryParse(component.TrimEnd('%'), NumberStyles.Float, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out var value) ? value : 0;

    private async Task OnChange(ChangeEventArgs args)
    {
        if (!ColorMath.TryParse(args.Value as string, out var h, out var s, out var v, out var a))
            return;
        await Context!.Root.SetAsync(h, s, v, Context.ShowAlpha ? a : Context.A);
        await Context.Root.CommitAsync();
    }

    // Focus lives on the GROUP (focus-within): the inner fields are chromeless segments. Hairlines
    // only BETWEEN channel fields (their subcontainer's divide-x) - the swatch dot sits flush.
    private const string GroupClasses =
        "bz-color-input-group flex min-w-0 items-stretch overflow-hidden " +
        "transition-[color,box-shadow] focus-within:border-ring focus-within:ring-2 focus-within:ring-ring/50 " +
        "has-disabled:pointer-events-none has-disabled:opacity-50";

    // Hex reads uppercase by convention; the transform is display-only, parsing is case-blind.
    private string TextClasses =>
        "bz-color-input h-full w-full min-w-0 grow bg-transparent font-mono outline-none " +
        "placeholder:text-muted-foreground" +
        (EffectiveFormat == ColorFormat.Hex ? " uppercase" : "");
}
